From b86be68764f20f6a5624b147f8388ebd3c9faacf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:19:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/18] nemotron: the latent top-k ranks every expert on a
 thread of its own, picks and ties as one warp's picks one at a time gave them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

tf_super_topk took a row's picks one argmax at a time on one warp, 40 µs a layer at decode. A block of ceil32(E)
threads now ranks each expert by how many others beat it (higher score, then lower id), so pick k is the expert k
others beat; once the finite scores run out every later pick is expert 0, as the old loop's repeated argmax over -inf
gave. Scores, sums and weights are the same operations in the same order. glue_ref.superTopk keeps the old rule as the
host reference, and the glue test covers 512 experts, 22 picks, 2 shares, rows 1/16/300, equal scores, fewer finite
scores than picks, and the norm on and off.
